Lota's Vulkan semaphores patch: one loop added to recreateSwapChain in
LÖVE's src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp. The present of each swap
chain image waits for a semaphore of that image, renderFinishedSemaphores
indexed by the image's index (lines 499 and 608). createSyncObjects makes
one for each image of the first swap chain (lines 3577-3582), once, when
setMode creates the device (line 743), and nothing makes more. A swap
chain made again by recreateSwapChain (lines 3685-3705) can have more
images than the first, and once the driver hands out the image the first
had none for, submitGpuCommands and present index past the end of the
semaphores with std::vector::at, which throws std::out_of_range, whose
message is "vector" (doc/contributors/upstream/024.md). A OnePlus Nord
N30 5G (Android 14, Adreno 619) made a first swap chain of 5 images with
vsync off, LÖVE's mailbox present mode there, and every later one of 6, so
a game on Vulkan with vsync off failed within a few frames of its first
swap chain rebuild, as LÖVE's own Android app does. This patch makes a
semaphore for each image a new swap chain adds, after createSwapChain, and
changes nothing else; a swap chain with fewer images leaves the extra
semaphores unused until a later one needs them, and cleanup destroys them
all as before (lines 3598-3600).

Nothing in Lota can do this: the semaphores, the swap chain, and the
present are private to LÖVE's Graphics, which no binding reaches, and a
game cannot choose how many images a driver gives a swap chain. CMake
applies the patch wherever it builds LÖVE's Vulkan renderer, on Linux,
Windows, and Android, to a copy of the file in the build tree
(ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love is never written to.

Drop this patch when LÖVE makes the semaphores of every swap chain it
creates.

diff -ruN a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
--- a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
@@ -3700,6 +3700,23 @@
 	createColorResources();
 	createDepthResources();
 
+	// The present of each swap chain image waits for a semaphore of its
+	// own, which createSyncObjects makes for the images of the first swap
+	// chain alone. A new one can have more images than the first (on an
+	// Android phone with vsync off, 6 where the first had 5), so make the
+	// semaphores of the images it adds, as Lota's patch does
+	// (ext/lota/engine/vulkan_semaphores.patch).
+	for (size_t i = renderFinishedSemaphores.size(); i < swapChainImages.size(); i++)
+	{
+		VkSemaphoreCreateInfo semaphoreInfo{};
+		semaphoreInfo.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_SEMAPHORE_CREATE_INFO;
+
+		VkSemaphore semaphore = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
+		if (vkCreateSemaphore(device, &semaphoreInfo, nullptr, &semaphore) != VK_SUCCESS)
+			throw love::Exception("Failed to create image available semaphore");
+		renderFinishedSemaphores.push_back(semaphore);
+	}
+
 	swapChainRequestFlags = SWAP_CHAIN_REQUEST_KEEP;
 	transitionColorDepthLayouts = true;
 }
